<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs dipped last week.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs dipped last week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe dipped slightly to 62 in the week to February 7 from 64 in the previous week, consultants Arthur Andersen said in a report.</p>
<p>U.K. rigs fell two to 31 and Norway slipped one to 17.</p>
<p>Dutch drilling rose one to 11 rigs. The Danish tally was steady at three rigs active.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
